What are Flame Resistant Plastics?
Flame resistant plastics are specialized polymer materials engineered to inhibit or resist combustion when exposed to fire or high temperatures. These materials incorporate additives or are chemically modified to achieve various fire safety ratings including HB, V0, V1, 5VB and 5VA classifications under UL 94 standards. They find critical applications across industries requiring stringent fire safety standards such as electrical/electronic components, automotive interiors, building materials and aerospace components.

These advanced materials function through multiple mechanisms including gas phase radical quenching, char formation, and endothermic decomposition to prevent flame propagation. Major product categories range from cost-effective HB grades for moderate risk applications to high-performance 5VA compounds for critical safety components.

